# Replace the tracked objects with the objects of another objects YAML, without
# restarting the node. The segmentation model stays loaded; one new FoundationPose
# TensorRT session is created per object of the new task.
#
# The YAML and every mesh it names are validated before anything changes. If that
# check fails, the current task keeps running and success is false. Once the switch
# starts, the old objects stop publishing at once (pose topics and TF frames).
#
# ``objects_cfg`` is an absolute path or a path relative to ROOT_DIR.
# ``reselect`` ignores the prompt cache next to the YAML and opens the prompt window.
# ``timeout`` is how long to wait, in seconds, for every new object to be registered
# and published. The wait does not count time spent in the prompt window. A timeout
# of 0 returns as soon as the request is validated and queued.
string objects_cfg
bool reselect
float32 timeout
---
bool success
string message
# tf_child_frame_id of every object of the new task, in objects-config order.
string[] tf_frames
